VeridianOS: kcmmetadatagenerator: fail when the output file cannot be opened

GCC reported ignoring return value of QFile::open [-Wunused-result] in
tools/kcmmetadatagenerator.cpp:54. Real bug: when the .desktop output could
not be opened, every write failed silently and the build tool still exited
0, leaving a missing or empty .desktop file for the KCM. It now reports the
file and QFile::errorString() with qCritical() and exits 1, exactly as the
tool already does when its input cannot be opened.

diff -ru a/tools/kcmmetadatagenerator.cpp b/tools/kcmmetadatagenerator.cpp
--- a/tools/kcmmetadatagenerator.cpp	2026-10-08 17:32:51.071642025 -0400
+++ b/tools/kcmmetadatagenerator.cpp	2026-10-08 17:32:51.165347179 -0400
@@ -51,7 +51,10 @@
     const QLatin1String namePrefix("Name");
 
     QFile out(app.arguments().at(2));
-    out.open(QIODevice::WriteOnly);
+    if (!out.open(QIODevice::WriteOnly)) {
+        qCritical() << "Could not open file" << out.fileName() << "for writing:" << out.errorString();
+        exit(1);
+    }
     out.write("[Desktop Entry]\n");
     out.write("Type=Application\n");
     out.write("NoDisplay=true\n");
